# Lib Module Rules

## Purpose
Core utilities, database configuration, authentication setup, and shared infrastructure code. This is the foundation layer of the application.

## Entry Points
- `src/lib/db/index.ts` - Database connection and Drizzle setup
- `src/lib/db/schema.ts` - Database schema definitions
- `src/lib/db/auth-schema.ts` - Authentication-related schema
- `src/lib/auth.ts` - BetterAuth configuration
- `src/lib/auth-client.ts` - Client-side auth utilities
- `src/lib/utils.ts` - Shared utility functions
- `src/lib/ratelimiter.ts` - Rate limiting configuration
- `src/lib/redis.ts` - Redis/Upstash configuration

## Allowed Imports
- Drizzle ORM packages
- BetterAuth packages
- Upstash Redis packages
- Postgres client
- Node.js built-ins (for server-side only)
- Zod for validation

## Forbidden Imports
- `@/components/*` - No React components
- `@/app/**` - No app route imports
- Client-side React libraries (in server-side files)

## Coding Conventions

### Database (Drizzle ORM)
- All database schemas in `src/lib/db/schema.ts`
- Use Drizzle ORM for all database operations
- Export `db` function from `src/lib/db/index.ts`
- Call `db()` to get database instance (lazy initialization)
- Use type-safe queries with schema imports

### Database Schema
```typescript
// Example: Schema definition
import { pgTable, text, timestamp } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";

export const user = pgTable("user", {
  id: text("id").primaryKey(),
  email: text("email").notNull().unique(),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at").defaultNow(),
});
```

### Database Queries
```typescript
// Example: Using db
import { db } from "@/lib/db";
import { user } from "@/lib/db/schema";
import { eq } from "drizzle-orm";

const users = await db().select().from(user).where(eq(user.email, email));
```

### Authentication
- BetterAuth configuration in `src/lib/auth.ts`
- Client-side auth utilities in `src/lib/auth-client.ts`
- Use BetterAuth API for session management
- Follow BetterAuth patterns and conventions

### Rate Limiting
- Configure rate limiter in `src/lib/ratelimiter.ts`
- Use Upstash Redis for rate limiting
- Export rate limiter instance for use in API routes

### Utilities
- Shared utility functions in `src/lib/utils.ts`
- Include `cn()` function for className merging
- Keep utilities pure and side-effect free
- Use TypeScript for all utilities

## AI Hints
- Use Drizzle ORM for all database operations (not Prisma)
- Keep database connection lazy-initialized
- Use type-safe Drizzle queries
- Follow BetterAuth patterns for authentication
- Keep utilities pure and testable
- Use environment variables for configuration
- Export functions, not instances (except for singletons like db)
